{"step_index":330,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T12:37:24Z","content":"Here is a breakdown of what that command does:\n\n---\n\n### What Each Part Does\n\n```bash\ngit push -u \\\n  -o merge_request.create \\\n  -o merge_request.target=main \\\n  -o merge_request.title=\"feat(inventory): move mtq-mailsrvp-01 to prod inventory\" \\\n  origin feat/move-mtq-mailsrvp-to-prod\n```\n\n1. **`git push origin feat/move-mtq-mailsrvp-to-prod`**:\n   * Uploads your local branch to the GitLab server (`gitsi.intranet.local`).\n   * This branch contains commit `b6f5e4b`:\n     - Cleaned `mtq-mailsrvp-01` out of [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml).\n     - Added `mtq-mailsrvp-01` into [`inventories/prod/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/prod/hosts.yml) under group `mail_servers`.\n\n2. **`-u` (`--set-upstream`)**:\n   * Links your local branch to `origin/feat/move-mtq-mailsrvp-to-prod` for automatic tracking.\n\n3. **`-o merge_request.create`**:\n   * This is a **GitLab Server Push Option** (`-o`). \n   * It tells GitLab to **automatically generate and open the Merge Request immediately** when the push arrives, saving you from having to manually open a browser tab, navigate to the page, and click *\"Create merge request\"*.\n\n4. **`-o merge_request.target=main`**:\n   * Tells GitLab to target the **`main`** branch for this Merge Request.\n\n5. **`-o merge_request.title=\"...\"`**:\n   * Pre-fills the title of the Merge Request in GitLab to match our conventional commit.\n\n---\n\n### In Short\nInstead of just pushing the branch and waiting for someone to manually create the MR on the web, this one command **publishes the branch and opens the GitLab Merge Request in one shot**.\n\nShall I run it?"}
