{"step_index":358,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T13:50:57Z","thinking":"**Creating Agent Configuration File**\n\nThe absence of the configuration file requires initiating its creation. This includes defining permanent guidelines for agent behavior, ensuring consistent interaction across conversations. The process involves generating a comprehensive `AGENTS.md` file, incorporating specific runbooks and strategies. Additionally, I need to check if the skill-specific configuration file (`SKILL.md`) requires updates to remain aligned with the agent's updated behaviors.\n\n\n**Defining Agent Operation Guidelines**\n\nDefining the agent's operational parameters is the immediate task. This involves establishing secure access credentials and the correct inventory structure. Dedicated groups and restricted environments will be used to ensure the agent's activities adhere to best practices.\n\nIt's crucial to specify how to automate infrastructure changes using version control, MRs, and specific push options. Verification and testing will use a dedicated script with template IDs for environments. The agent will strictly follow PROD guidelines including zero downtime and human confirmation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > ~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md\n# Global Rules & Memory — Antigravity\n\n## Server Onboarding to IaC & Semaphore (Standard Operating Procedure)\n\nThis workflow is permanently recorded for onboarding any new or legacy server into `infra-management-system` and Semaphore.\n\n### 1. Zone & Network Reality (Hard Rule)\n* **Never mix network zones**: Inter-VLAN corporate firewalls strictly isolate DEV runners from PROD subnets.\n* Hosts with PROD naming (`*p-*`) or on PROD subnets (e.g. `172.30.39.0/24`, `172.30.230-231.0/24`) **must** be placed in `inventories/prod/hosts.yml`.\n* **Runner routing**:\n  - `dev` -> `th2-ansid-run1` (DEV VLANs `172.30.242-243.0/24`)\n  - `PROD` -> `th2-ansip-run1` (`172.30.199.225`, routes to datacenter & Martinique PROD)\n\n### 2. Runner SSH Key & Host Setup (`spui-runner`)\n* **SSH Port**: `30`\n* **Account**: `spui-runner`, group `SSH_Users` (in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` AllowGroups).\n* **Sudoers**: `/etc/sudoers.d/spui-runner` with `spui-runner ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL`.\n* **Authorized Keys** in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`:\n  - **PROD**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFW7ywu9PSVguYkbxDRMkU8FH/Ws09CDTWUSylusKkDA semaphore-runner-prod`\n  - **DEV / VAL**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner`\n* **Manual bootstrap script**: `playbooks/bootstrap-spui-runner-manual.sh <zone>`.\n* **Warning**: Never close the active root/superuser session before verifying `spui-runner` login due to `AllowGroups`.\n\n### 3. Inventory Declaration Pattern\n* In `inventories/<env>/hosts.yml`:\n  ```yaml\n  all:\n    hosts:\n      <hostname>:\n        ansible_host: <ip>\n        ansible_port: 30\n        ansible_user: spui-runner\n    children:\n      <dedicated_group>:\n        hosts:\n          <hostname>:\n  ```\n* **Isolation**: Keep new hosts OUT of shared application groups (`frontaux`, `backends`, `databases`) unless explicitly requested.\n* **Validate locally**:\n  ```bash\n  ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --graph\n  ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --host <hostname>\n  ```\n\n### 4. Git & Automated Merge Request\n* 1 subject = 1 branch = 1 MR.\n* Automatically publish and create the MR in one shot via GitLab push options:\n  ```bash\n  git checkout -b feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n  git add inventories/<env>/hosts.yml\n  git commit -m \"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\"\n  git push -u -o merge_request.create -o merge_request.target=main -o merge_request.title=\"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\" origin feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n  ```\n\n### 5. Semaphore Verification\n* Once merged, Semaphore's inventory follows `main`.\n* Execute read-only fact gathering via `playbooks/check-distro-kernel.yml` with `--limit <hostname>`:\n  - PROD: Template ID `131` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - PROD (recon)*)\n  - DEV: Template ID `130` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - DEV*)\n* Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\nEOF","Cwd":"/home/koby","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Write global AGENTS.md memory file"}}]}
