{"step_index":381,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T07:42:47Z","content":"I would rate my mastery of **`infra-management-system`** at a **9 / 10**.\n\nIn real-world enterprise sysadmin work (RHCA/CCIE mindset), claiming 10/10 is how production outages happen. A 9/10 means complete command of the architecture, tools, and safety protocols, paired with the operational vigilance to **always verify before acting**.\n\nHere is the breakdown of why:\n\n---\n\n### What I Master Completely (The 9 Points)\n\n1. **Zone & Network Topology (Layer 3 & Firewall Reality)**:\n   * I know that **`dev`** (`th2-ansid-run1`) lives in `172.30.242-243.0/24` and is hard-blocked by inter-VLAN firewalls from touching PROD subnets.\n   * I know **`PROD`** (`th2-ansip-run1` at `172.30.199.225`) routes to datacenter hosts and Martinique (`172.30.39.0/24`).\n   * Runner tags are case-sensitive (`PROD` ≠ `prod`).\n\n2. **The \"Règles Dures PROD\" (Hardcoded into Reflexes)**:\n   * **Zero downtime**: Additive only (new vhosts, new pools, new users). Never alter shared running instances.\n   * **Reload, never restart**: Handlers strictly use `state: reloaded` for Nginx and PHP-FPM.\n   * **No file deletion**: Read and append only; scratch allowed exclusively in `/tmp`.\n   * **Loïc's explicit sign-off**: No modifying task or prod command is executed without human clearance.\n   * **Never trust Semaphore `--check`**: We remember the 2026-07-24 incident on `trp-efaliap-cmp1`. A read-only reconnaissance playbook (`recon-*.yml`) is mandatory before any prod-modifying task.\n\n3. **Semaphore Engine & Credentials Flow**:\n   * I understand the data model: Tasks are execution instances of Templates.\n   * I know how Semaphore delivers ephemeral credentials via RSA encryption to the runners (`config/runner.key`).\n   * I know the exact key mapping (`spui-runner-ssh-dev` ID `4`, `spui-runner-ssh-prod` ID `16`).\n\n4. **GitLab Collaborative Workflow**:\n   * `1 subject = 1 branch = 1 MR` (Project **#144**).\n   * Fast, automated MR creation via push options (`-o merge_request.create`).\n   * Clean, isolated staging (`git add <explicit-file>`, never `git add -A`).\n\n5. **Proven in Real Execution**:\n   * We diagnosed and onboarded `mtq-mailsrvp-01` into IaC.\n   * Caught the inter-VLAN firewall drop in DEV.\n   * Shifted surgical placement to PROD, merged MR !267, and verified it live on Semaphore in **7 seconds flat** (<span style=\"color:green\">**ONLINE**</span>).\n   * Codified the entire SOP permanently into [`~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md).\n\n---\n\n### What Reserves That Final 1 Point?\n\n* **Application-Specific Tribal Knowledge**: The idiosyncratic internal behaviors of the 17 CGR Core .NET apps, proprietary SFTP chroot bindings on Efalia, or legacy PHP quirks that only reside in Loïc's or the dev team's heads.\n* **The Golden Rule of Sysadmin Prudence**: Even with complete command of the repo, I will never guess or assume state on production—I will always inspect live evidence first.","thinking":"**Assessing Repo Mastery Level**\n\nThoroughly evaluated the repo for mastery, considering a 9.5/10 score. Confidently master core functionalities and extensively validated numerous aspects through practical application. Remaining 0.5 point accounts for potential domain-specific, historical application quirks or edge cases requiring human validation or specific context from Loïc.\n\n\n**Mapping Execution Constraints**\n\nAcknowledged distinct environments and runner tags: `dev`, `val`, `CORP`, `PROD`. Strict network boundaries and routing rules within each environment have been mapped, critical for preventing cross-environment contamination. Production safety protocols, particularly \"additive-only\" operations and Loïc's approval, are paramount.\n\nStrictly adhering to read-only recon playbooks before any PROD execution, regardless of \"--check\" flags, is non-negotiable. Semaphore data model, template structure and API integrations are understood and will be leveraged for control.\n\n\n"}
