* Task #914 failed with <span style=\"color:red\">**`ssh: connect to host 172.30.39.153 port 30: Operation timed out`**</span>.\n  * **Root Cause Identified**: The host firewall was open, but the corporate **inter-VLAN firewall strictly blocks the DEV runner** (`th2-ansid-run1` in `172.30.242.x`) from routing into the Martinique PROD subnet (`172.30.39.0/24`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Moving to PROD & Total Victory\n* **Realignment**:\n  * Created branch `feat/move-mtq-mailsrvp-to-prod`.\n  * Removed `mtq-mailsrvp-01` from DEV and added it to [`inventories/prod/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/prod/hosts.yml) under an isolated `mail_servers` group (ensuring standard web/db playbooks never touch it).\n  * Auto-created **MR !267** in one shot via git push options (`-o merge_request.create`), which was approved and merged into `main`.\n* **The Live Semaphore Test**:\n  * Created Template `131` (*`Check Linux Distro and Kernel - PROD (recon)`*).\n  * Triggered **Task #915** with `--limit mtq-mailsrvp-01` dispatched to the **PROD runner** (**`th2-ansip-run1`**).\n  * **Result**: Finished in **7 seconds flat** with <span style=\"color:green\">**SUCCESS**</span>! \n  * `mtq-mailsrvp-01` reported <span style=\"color:green\">**ONLINE**</span> on Debian 13.6 (Kernel `6.12.95+deb13-amd64`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Codified into Permanent Memory\nTo ensure we execute future server onboardings in minutes without re-learning the pitfalls:\n* Documented the complete 5-step Standard Operating Procedure directly in [`~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md) (network reality check, `spui-runner` key setup, surgical inventory declaration, one-shot GitLab MR push, and fast Semaphore verification).\n\n---\n\nEverything in the repo is clean, fast-forwarded to `origin/main` at `81767ed`, and ready for our next mission!","thinking":"**Recalling agent integration process**\n\nInitial integration involved adapting a sysadmin agent definition from an external code platform. Registration occurred within the Antigravity system as a global skill accessible through a specific invocation syntax. This adaptation marked the initial onboarding step for the external agent.\n\n\n**Assessing initial infrastructure landscape**\n\nThe system's infrastructure management resides within a specific code repository, organized across multiple environments including 'dev', 'val', 'corp', and 'prod'. Strict \"hard production safety rules\" must be adhered to in the production environment. A central configuration file governs access to the infrastructure management control plane.\n\nThe target mail server, 'mtq-mailsrvp-01', appears accessible with identified services. The server already has an existing runner, initially configured only for the production environment. Now, attempting onboarding into the development zone requires adding a development runner key to the mail server.\n\n\n"}
